<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33875" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλλοψ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οπος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, epith. of fish
		(exc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλλοπι κούρᾳ</span>, of Echo, <i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			<u>Syrinx</u>
			18
		</span></i>), expld. as <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dumb</i>
			by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (also by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δασεῖς, τραχεῖς,
			ποικίλοι</span>), but perh. rather, <i>scaly</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεπίς</span>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλλοπας ἰχθῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					212
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλλοπος μυνδοῦ δίκην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1375
				</span></i>
			:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλλοπος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				117
			</span></i>: or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλλός</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχθύες ἐλλοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Titanomach.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλλοῖς ἰχθύσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					1297
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., <i>fish</i>, in general, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				481
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				600
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.658
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.55
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				89
			</span></i>; fem., <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				796
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> an unknown
				<i>sea-fish</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				505a15
			</span></i>, etc.; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλοψ</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archestr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				11.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Matro
				<u>Conv.</u>
				69
			</span></i>, Apio ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.294f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.979c
			</span></i>; identified with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερὸς
			ἰχθῦς</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				8.28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> a
			<i>serpent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				490
			</span></i>.</div>
